  "step_3": "The decision reason based on variance requires comparing the statistical spread of outcomes. The individual did not refer to variance, standard deviation, or any measure of dispersion. Instead, they focused on the probability of loss (50% in B vs. 25% in A) and the magnitude of the loss (higher in A). While both lotteries have the same expected value (-1500), the individual’s justification is based on the probability of loss and loss magnitude, not on variance. Although the variance-based reason would favor B (lower variance), the individual’s reasoning does not align with this rule. The information considered (probability of loss, magnitude) is not equivalent to variance. The justification does not reference or imply a comparison of variances. Therefore, the decision reason based on variance was not used by the individual.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

